{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-16T22:58:09.756Z","author":"pi-ops-292","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"f92080cc29f1e8c791774009","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-16T22:58:09.756Z","author":"pi-ops-292","text":"Root cause (issue #292): prepare renders the pending version's heading with --date-from-version, so a resumed candidate (version day before today) is stamped with its version day. The release step then tags it today; pm-changelog by design derives a tagged window's heading from the tag commit date (pm-changelog#120), so post-tag regeneration on unchanged main renders a different day and changelog:check is red on main. The release PR's own CI passes (candidate still untagged), so the failure only appears after the merge.\n\nDesign: use the generator's existing --date-fallback flag (applies only while no release tag exists; ignored once the tag exists, so it matches post-tag invocations byte-for-byte). decideDailyRelease now outputs heading_date: today in RELEASE_TIMEZONE, padded ISO, when the version's calendar day is before today; empty for a same-day release, which is therefore unchanged. The 'Generate changelog and release notes' step, in the same in-place package.json policy rewrite that already appends --include-empty, swaps --date-from-version for --date-fallback <heading_date> in the three changelog scripts when resumed, refreshes a stale pin when a candidate is re-prepared on a later day, and restores --date-from-version when the pending version is current again. The release commit carries the pinned spelling, so the release PR's CI (untagged candidate), prepare's nested release:check and post-tag checks on main all regenerate the same bytes with no follow-up regeneration. The date verifier accepts a pinned --date-fallback day (explicit ISO day only) as an equally clock-free alternative to --date-from-version. Rust/justfile releases (CHANGELOG_DATE derived from the tag name) keep their own spelling and are not touched."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-16T22:58:09.756Z"}],"before_hash":"51839118011bdb7ed4d82e217685c7366a64526aaadb0b3eeffaf3cc20405bfc","after_hash":"595a2ae4c062da383ce15bb31ceae48da8abf7f0d83ae7c680fae08d7a172b87","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"8a2f6331861e2526948e3f13b18076ea9006cb8bec463ccf5a20832fabfb4853"}
